- RR-03 | medium | attribution | “alpha_850 … 4 in the shown lines” | At least five distinct bibcodes explicitly specify alpha_850 in the rebuilt parameter/assumption lists: 2017ApJ...837..150S, 2017ApJ...844..123F, 2022ApJ...929..100K, 2023MNRAS.524..923Z and 2025A&A...694A.218B. | Recount and publish the counted bibcodes.
- RR-04 | medium | stale | “3.6 … (10 papers)” in parameters.md | This retains the earlier census while omitting explicit rebuilt-pack adopters, including 2017MNRAS.468.4205K, 2020MNRAS.495.1760O, 2020ApJ...902..113I, 2023ApJ...953...75H, 2025ApJ...988..182N and 2025ApJ...989..115T. | Refresh the list and its count; distinguish illustrative examples from a complete census.
- RR-05 | medium | attribution | “1.1: 2015ApJ...812L..23S” | No supplied pack line supports that attribution; the skill itself instead describes this paper’s dynamical values as 0.6 and 1.6. A supported 1.1 adoption appears in the assumptions for 2019ApJ...881...43K. | Replace the example with 2019ApJ...881...43K, or supply evidence for the original attribution.
- RR-06 | medium | attribution | “PDR Toolbox … cloudy” with example 2017MNRAS.466.2825B | That excerpt’s step 5 explicitly names **3d-pdr**, not either tool in this row. | Move this example to a separate 3d-pdr entry.
- RR-07 | medium | stale | “[CI] Tex … 26 to 31.8 K” | The rebuilt assumptions explicitly give “[CI] Tex = 25 K” for 2025ApJ...993L..40S. | Extend the range to include 25 K and add the supporting example.
- RR-08 | medium | stale | “r21 … 0.4 to 1.12 overall”; “r31 … 0.27 to 0.97 in galaxies” | The pack gives an observed r21 range of 0.4–1.2 in 2020MNRAS.498.1560J and optically thin r21 ≈ 3–4 in 2018ApJ...867..111Z; r31 = 1.0 is explicitly adopted in 2022MNRAS.514.2346K. | Refresh the bounds and separate ordinary, nuclear and optically thin cases.
- RR-09 | medium | stale | “r41 … 0.31 to 0.91” | The pack gives r41 = 0.22 ± 0.11 for the tail in 2024A&A...689A..67G and r41 = 1 for the QSO in 2020MNRAS.493.3744F. The row’s 0.91 example is r43, a different ratio. | Split r41 and r43 into separate rows and refresh their ranges.
- RR-10 | medium | stale | “r61 0.34 … to 0.64”; “r71 0.16 … to 0.48” | Rebuilt assumptions give r61 = 0.92 and r71 = 0.65 in 2025A&A...695A..23S, and conservative r71 = 0.1 in 2026ApJ...997..218A. | Label the existing numbers specifically as the 2020A&A...636A..37D comparison SLEDs; add the broader adopted range separately.
- RR-11 | medium | stale | “CO/H2 … 1.6e-5 … to 7e-4” | The pack explicitly gives CO/H2 ≈ 1e-3 for carbon-rich ejecta in 2018MNRAS.481.4931E; parameters.md already includes it. | Include 1e-3 or explicitly exclude evolved-star ejecta from this row.
- RR-12 | medium | attribution | “26 K from the [CI] line ratio” | For 2021A&A...654L...8C, the pack says “[CI](2-1)/[CI](1-0) = 0.47 (Tex = 26 K) … from literature averages.” This is adopted, not measured for that target. | Label both the ratio and temperature as literature assumptions.
- RR-13 | medium | unsupported | “aperture enclosing all >=3 sigma emission” | The cited pack lines do not establish this as a universal extraction rule. The pack also documents completeness-oriented broad masks (2021A&A...650A.134P) and masks constructed from smoothed cubes (2024MNRAS.528.6768H). | Present aperture/mask selection as a justified choice; require growth-curve and noise checks without imposing a universal 3-sigma boundary.
- RR-14 | medium | broken-edit | “[CI](1-0) … M_H2 = 1375.8 …”; later “treat it as helium-inclusive” | The executable equation is labelled H2-only while the following explanation identifies it as including helium. The pack explicitly distinguishes the helium-free 9.51e-5 expression in 2025ApJ...987..158F from mu = 1.36 in 2021ApJ...909..181L. | Relabel the 1375.8 expressions M_mol, including the [CI](2-1) expression, and give H2-only conversion explicitly.
- RR-15 | medium | science | “the LTE mass traces only part … so the derived alpha_CO is a lower bound” | The fraction-of-total limitation belongs to the particular analysis in 2017ApJ...848..101V. It does not establish a guaranteed lower bound for every LTE estimate with uncertain abundance, opacity and excitation. | Restrict the statement to that paper’s sampled gas and make any lower-bound interpretation conditional on the adopted model.
- RR-16 | medium | omission | “per pixel from a RADEX grid fit” | The offered route omits consequential steps explicitly documented in 2024ApJ...971..176H: linewidth rescaling, correction for the induced alpha_CO sampling prior, grid-boundary checks and the selection bias toward regions with both 13CO detections. | Add a short validation requirement and move the detailed procedure to parameters.md.
- RR-17 | medium | omission | “Dust RJ continuum: M_mol = L_nu(850 um rest) / alpha_850” | The applicability conditions are incomplete. The pack specifies optically thin RJ emission in 2025ApJ...987..158F and restricts a Scoville application to lambda_rest > 250 um in 2020MNRAS.498.4109J. | Require checking rest wavelength and optical depth, and specify the temperature/SED extrapolation used to obtain L_nu(850 um).
- RR-18 | medium | omission | “Write the error budget” | Distance uncertainty is omitted despite the pack explicitly noting L ∝ D² and median distance uncertainty ≈ 7% in 2022MNRAS.510.4998Z. | Include distance and magnification uncertainties when material, alongside flux, excitation and conversion-factor terms.
- RR-19 | medium | usability | “scale the per-beam noise by the number of independent beams” | The instruction leaves the scaling operation unspecified and can be read as multiplication by N_beams. The cited 2020ApJ...897L..19M supplies N_box and N_beam. | Write sigma_ap ≈ sigma_beam sqrt(N_box/N_beam), with assumptions, or prefer directly measured aperture-spectrum noise.
- RR-20 | low | length | SKILL.md exceeds roughly 300 lines | Long population tables, software counts, example inventories and source-card summaries obscure the execution path. | Move detailed ranges, counted bibcode lists and software inventories to references/parameters.md; retain essential equations and checks in SKILL.md.

## Notes

The description’s 876-paper count matches the rebuilt pack.
The refreshed software counts largely match; restoring MyRadex, imfit and GILDAS is supported by new evidence, not a demonstrated lost fix.
The principal reconciliation safeguards remain present; incomplete range and reference refreshes prevent COMPLETE.
